PART 2: ESTABLISH A PROFESSIONAL DESIGN DIRECTION

Brand identity

Use the official Swiftvero logo as the single source of truth.

Official brand colours:

* Primary cyan: #00B4D8
* Secondary cyan: #90E0EF
* Light cyan: #CAF0F8
* White: #FFFFFF

Use dark neutral colours for text and appropriate neutral colours for backgrounds, borders and surfaces.

Do not introduce unrelated colours or create a new brand identity.

Visual design principles

The website must look:

* Premium.
* Professional.
* Realistic.
* Trustworthy.
* Clean.
* Modern.
* Well organised.
* Easy to understand.
* Mobile-first.
* Appropriate for an international logistics company.

Use a restrained colour system.

White and neutral backgrounds should dominate. Use the primary cyan for important actions, selected states and meaningful highlights.

Do not fill every section with cyan backgrounds.

Avoid excessive rounded cards, giant decorative icons, unnecessary floating shapes, gradient backgrounds and decorative pills.

Use cards only when they genuinely improve the organisation of information.

Prefer clean sections, clear headings, well-aligned content, meaningful whitespace and subtle borders.

Do not put every sentence inside a separate card.

Do not use excessive shadows.

Use consistent corner radii instead of randomly mixing different shapes.

The overall interface should resemble a carefully designed premium logistics platform, not a generic SaaS dashboard template.

Typography

The current typography feels too large and visually crowded on mobile.

Review the entire typography system.

Use a modern readable font such as Inter, provided it works consistently with the existing project.

Recommended mobile typography:

* Main hero heading: approximately 30–36px.
* Section heading: approximately 22–27px.
* Card heading: approximately 16–19px.
* Body text: approximately 14–16px.
* Secondary information: approximately 12–14px.
* Small labels: approximately 11–12px.

Use these as starting points, not fixed values for every element.

Use responsive typography and appropriate line heights.

Do not make every heading bold and oversized.

Reduce unnecessary text weight and improve the balance between headings and body content.

Use clear visual hierarchy so visitors immediately understand what matters.

Do not make users zoom in or scroll excessively to understand simple information.

