Use helpful descriptions and appropriate placeholders.

Keep the form compact and mobile-friendly.

Pricing calculations

The quotation engine must support:

* Actual weight.
* Volumetric weight.
* Billable weight.
* Destination-based pricing.
* Available carrier services.
* Fuel or other applicable surcharges.
* Taxes.
* Approved additional fees.
* Currency handling.
* Rate expiry and quote validity.

Use the actual carrier pricing rules and verified account rate information where available.

Never invent live carrier rates.

Never use hardcoded sample prices as real customer quotations.

When accurate carrier pricing is unavailable, label the result as an estimate rather than a confirmed final rate.

Clearly explain that final shipping costs may change after the package is inspected, weighed and measured.

Show a clear breakdown of charges.

Do not add arbitrary line items such as jet fuel, airport security or screening fees unless they genuinely apply to that shipment and are supported by the pricing configuration.

Do not confuse estimated weight with the verified facility weight.

